{#
/**
 * @file
 * Shared spacing utility-class builder for the Jarvis SDCs.
 *
 * Maps the padding/margin/vertical_padding/no_padding props every component
 * repeats onto the jp-* utility classes in css/overrides.css. Imported as
 * `{% import '@jarvis/jarvis-spacing.html.twig' as jarvis %}` — call sites
 * pass |default()-guarded props so undefined props are safe under
 * strict_variables. One source of truth: change spacing behaviour here.
 *
 * vertical_padding fallbacks are FALSE everywhere. Canvas ignores a prop's
 * schema `default` and seeds a placed component from `examples[0]`, so a prop
 * with no examples arrives omitted; a `true` fallback then padded sections
 * whose toggle read off until the editor flipped it on and back off — the
 * toggle and the rendered spacing disagreed. Keep the two in step: to make a
 * component default to padded, give vertical_padding `examples: [true]` (the
 * 1/2/3-column components do) and leave the fallback FALSE, so an absent prop
 * still matches an unchecked box.
 *
 * no_padding is the last argument and Section is the only component that
 * declares that prop, so every other caller omits it and it arrives null
 * (falsy). Passing `no_padding|default(false)` from components that never
 * define the prop only hardcoded false at 14 call sites.
 */
#}
{% macro classes(padding, padding_size, margin, margin_size, vertical_padding, no_padding) -%}
  {{- [
    padding != 'none' ? 'jp-p-' ~ padding ~ '-' ~ padding_size : '',
    margin != 'none' ? 'jp-m-' ~ margin ~ '-' ~ margin_size : '',
    vertical_padding ? 'jp-vpad' : '',
    no_padding ? 'jp-nopad' : '',
  ]|join(' ')|trim -}}
{%- endmacro %}
